```js
export function solve(nums, target) {
  let lo = 0;
  let hi = nums.length;

  while (lo < hi) {
    const mid = Math.floor((lo + hi) / 2);
    if (nums[mid] < target) {
      lo = mid + 1;
    } else {
      hi = mid;
    }
  }

  return lo;
}
```

The restored invariant is that every index below lo contains a value less than target, and every array index at or above hi contains a value at least target. Initializing hi to nums.length keeps the end insertion position available; each iteration shrinks the interval until lo equals the required index. Empty input returns 0 without accessing an element; no dependencies, API changes, or test edits are needed.

